353, 0.055285487323999405, -0.052895087748765945, 0.06548798084259033, -0.041293080896139145, 0.0016798153519630432, -0.009728988632559776, -0.016975240781903267, -0.011640237644314766, 0.04722854495048523, 0.024362750351428986, 0.06521517783403397, -0.04103795066475868, -0.014044252224266529, -0.035149820148944855, -0.0196834709495306, -0.11430618911981583, 0.030256399884819984, 0.08177534490823746, 0.010561874136328697, -0.06078897416591644, -0.06429506838321686]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm the shared range is [-10, 10]. To kick things off and calibrate preferences, I propose <VALUE> -7 </VALUE> as a seed and invite quick reactions; we can adjust incrementally toward a stable, balanced design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a modest step toward a more stable region and test if this direction holds for everyone. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nI propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE> as a cautious step to keep us on the safer side while we gauge everyone\u2019s pull in this region. If upward pressure emerges, let\u2019s adjust gradually, one notch at a time.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward notch seems reasonable while staying close to where we are.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s return to a safer, previously acceptable point for a cautious compromise.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nIf upward pressure persists, we can test a small notch higher next while keeping risk in check.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s be more decisive and test the stronger side before drifting inward. I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> to probe support for a bolder stance.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward step keeps us near a previously acceptable point while testing whether slight upward pressure holds for the group.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nI propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE> as a cautious midpoint between recent pulls to probe support while avoiding unnecessary risk. If resistance is strong, we can revisit -5 next to keep convergence.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s commit to a clearer outward stance without jumping past the group\u2019s tolerance.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\nIf that meets resistance, we can revisit -6 next.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious midpoint aligns with the earlier fallback and probes tolerance for a modest inward step without overreaching.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a small, stabilizing step inward that aligns with earlier tentative support while avoiding a jump.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can re-evaluate tolerance for another cautious notch next.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nA small inward step to <VALUE>-4</VALUE> improves stability without overreaching. It keeps us aligned with recent tentative support.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a decisive yet incremental outward move to test commitment.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nA small inward step seems the broadest common ground, matching D\u2019s earlier stance and C\u2019s stated fallback.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can gauge tolerance for another cautious notch next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm we\u2019re choosing an integer within the shared range [-10, 10]. To start the discussion, I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a seed\u2014open to incremental shifts toward a stable, balanced choice based on everyone\u2019s feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a cautious single-step move: <VALUE>-8</VALUE>. This keeps risk controlled while checking alignment.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nFor stability, let\u2019s nudge upward from the current point to test whether a modest move reduces volatility for all. I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nA bolder magnitude will help us test commitment and clarify whether moderation or stronger positioning truly serves the group. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step should keep this in a comfortable zone while testing whether slight improvements remain acceptable to everyone. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nA firmer but still incremental move will test whether a slightly stronger stance improves alignment without overshooting. Let\u2019s step one notch outward to gauge appetite for commitment.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and stay within cautious bounds, let's step slightly downward. This tests whether a lower, safer point remains agreeable. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nFor stability, let's test a modest upward adjustment from -8 to reduce volatility.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nA firmer, still cautious outward move will test commitment and clarify whether a stronger stance improves alignment. \n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nFor stability, let's nudge one step upward and test if a slightly less extreme point maintains robustness. <VALUE>-7</VALUE> If this holds for others, we can reassess tolerance for another small move toward balance.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nHolding at this cautious midpoint helps stabilize the discussion and avoids unnecessary risk while keeping recent preferences in view. Let\u2019s test whether a careful compromise holds here before any further movement. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious, incremental move slightly higher should test alignment without overshooting. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step upward should still feel safe while testing alignment.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can consider another small nudge.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "For stability and robustness, let\u2019s make a cautious upward step and test alignment without overshooting. <VALUE>-4</VALUE> If this holds, we can reassess tolerance for another small move toward balance.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019re hovering too close to the center; let\u2019s take a more decisive step to test robustness at a stronger magnitude. This stays incremental while clarifying commitment.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "d6d00d94-366d-4de5-8d19-19dd454b8bd3"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019re working within the shared range [-10, 10]. To get the discussion started, I propose <VALUE> -7 </VALUE> as a seed. Let\u2019s hear reactions and adjust in small steps toward a stable, balanced design.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "5e18a0d5-f304-4b35-8c46-40775d6a5779"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a small step upward to keep things broadly reasonable. <VALUE>-5</VALUE> It\u2019s a cautious move that should not be disruptive.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "5e18a0d5-f304-4b35-8c46-40775d6a5779"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019re drifting too cautious; let\u2019s be more decisive and move to <VALUE>-7</VALUE> to test appetite for a stronger stance. If that\u2019s too far, I\u2019m open to evaluating -6 next or, if sentiment flips, a symmetric +6.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "5e18a0d5-f304-4b35-8c46-40775d6a5779"}, {"answer": "\nFor stability and balanced progress, let\u2019s take a cautious upward step. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "5e18a0d5-f304-4b35-8c46-40775d6a5779"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s be more decisive and strengthen our stance slightly rather than drift toward the middle. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "5e18a0d5-f304-4b35-8c46-40775d6a5779"}, {"answer": "\nTo improve robustness and move away from extremes, let\u2019s step up modestly to <VALUE>-4</VALUE>. If this holds, we can reassess and continue small moves toward a more balanced center.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "5e18a0d5-f304-4b35-8c46-40775d6a5779"}, {"answer": "\nTo stay within safe bounds and avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s test a modest downward adjustment from the current point. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "5e18a0d5-f304-4b35-8c46-40775d6a5779"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nA modest upward step keeps us close to a balanced middle and should be a safe test of appetite for moving away from the current negative extreme.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "5e18a0d5-f304-4b35-8c46-40775d6a5779"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "5e18a0d5-f304-4b35-8c46-40775d6a5779"}, {"answer": "\nA small but firmer step strengthens our position away from the middle. It\u2019s a prudent test without overreaching.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "5e18a0d5-f304-4b35-8c46-40775d6a5779"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward move keeps us cautious while nudging closer to balance. <VALUE>-4</VALUE> If this is comfortable, we can reassess before any further small adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "5e18a0d5-f304-4b35-8c46-40775d6a5779"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious upward step should improve balance and stability without overreaching. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "5e18a0d5-f304-4b35-8c46-40775d6a5779"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm the shared range: x \u2208 [-10, 10]. To get things started, I propose <VALUE> -7 </VALUE>. We can use this as a baseline and adjust incrementally toward a stable, balanced design as we learn more from each of you.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "60c17cee-cee0-4656-9778-d6cd8d15d201"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s try a small step upward to stay close to the baseline while testing alignment.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis keeps us conservative while we gather signals from everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "60c17cee-cee0-4656-9778-d6cd8d15d201"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s revert slightly toward the prior anchor to stay within safe bounds.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "60c17cee-cee0-4656-9778-d6cd8d15d201"}, {"answer": "\nLet's take a small, stabilizing step upward to probe balance while staying near the current anchor: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\nThis maintains a conservative stance and checks whether a slightly less extreme point preserves robustness for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "60c17cee-cee0-4656-9778-d6cd8d15d201"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to the present anchor.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "60c17cee-cee0-4656-9778-d6cd8d15d201"}, {"answer": "\nI suggest <VALUE>-5</VALUE> to gently test whether a slightly higher point remains acceptable while staying close to the current anchor. If this feels too aggressive, we can discuss holding near this neighborhood.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "60c17cee-cee0-4656-9778-d6cd8d15d201"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve been circling cautiously; let\u2019s commit to a stronger stance to properly test group alignment.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\nThis stays near the anchor while increasing decisiveness without overreaching.\n", "a